body:
The following test case is failing because our identity hash func creates a recursive cycle, and we're not able to distinguish between the cycle caused by `foo(1)` and the one caused by `foo(2)`.

```
    def test_recursive_hash_func(self):
        def hash_int(x):
            return x

        [USER].cache(hash_funcs={int: hash_int})
        def foo(x):
            return x

        self.assertNotEqual(foo(2), foo(1))
```
